# systemd's EFI stub with the SP11 patch: the first part of the signed boot image that
# scripts/25-build-secureboot-rpms.sh packs for each kernel (docs/secure-boot.md). A build input: the package is
# never installed on the device, step 25 takes the stub out of it.
#
# Only the stub is built. Fedora's own patches to systemd do not touch src/boot, so the source is the tarball
# of Fedora's source RPM plus the patch; the configuration is Fedora's for the boot loader part (release mode,
# TPM measurements, the SBAT entries taken from the build root's os-release), with every optional feature of
# the rest of systemd switched off, which keeps the build requirements short and the result independent of
# what the build root happens to hold.
%global debug_package %{nil}
%global __meson_auto_features disabled

Name:           sp11-secureboot-stub
Version:        @VERSION@
Release:        @RELEASE@%{?dist}
Summary:        systemd-stub for the Surface Pro 11's signed boot images (build input)
License:        LGPL-2.1-or-later
URL:            https://systemd.io
ExclusiveArch:  aarch64
Source0:        systemd-%{version}.tar.gz
Patch1:         0001-stub-start-the-kernel-without-LoadImage-and-read-the-initramfs.patch

BuildRequires:  gcc
BuildRequires:  meson
BuildRequires:  ninja-build
BuildRequires:  gperf
BuildRequires:  patch
BuildRequires:  libcap-devel
BuildRequires:  libmount-devel
BuildRequires:  libxcrypt-devel
BuildRequires:  python3
BuildRequires:  python3dist(jinja2)
BuildRequires:  python3dist(pyelftools)

%description
systemd's EFI stub @VERSION@ (linuxaa64.efi.stub) with one patch for the Surface Pro 11: the stub starts the
kernel itself instead of handing it to shim's loader, which does not return on this firmware, and with
sp11_initrd=<path> on the command line it reads the initramfs from the ESP.
Inputs: @INPUTS@

%prep
%autosetup -n systemd-%{version} -p1

%build
%meson -Dmode=release -Defi=true -Dtpm=true -Db_ndebug=false -Dbootloader=enabled \
       -Dversion-tag=@VERSION_TAG@
ninja -C %{_vpath_builddir} -v src/boot/linuxaa64.efi.stub

%install
install -D -m 0644 %{_vpath_builddir}/src/boot/linuxaa64.efi.stub \
        %{buildroot}%{_prefix}/lib/sp11/secureboot/linuxaa64.efi.stub

%files
%license LICENSE.LGPL2.1
%{_prefix}/lib/sp11/secureboot/linuxaa64.efi.stub

%changelog
* Fri Nov 20 2026 SP11 build <sp11@localhost> - @VERSION@-@RELEASE@
- systemd-stub with the Surface Pro 11 patch
